# Git: commit and push every change

This project's remote is `origin` → https://github.com/Vshah513/Eastwick-Boston.git on branch `main`.

After finishing any set of file changes in this workspace:

1. `git add -A`
2. `git commit -m "<short summary of what changed>"`
3. `git push origin main`

- Never push to any other repository or branch.
- Keep `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `.env*`, and build output out of commits (use `.gitignore`).
- If the push fails (auth, conflicts), stop and tell the user instead of force-pushing.
